= Probability — Simple =

'''Probability''' is a way to describe how likely an event is or how uncertain we are.

Probabilities usually run from 0 to 1.

A probability of 0 means an event is treated as impossible in the model.

A probability of 1 means it is treated as certain.

Probability has precise mathematical rules.

But there are different ideas about what a probability means. It can represent long-run frequency, physical chance, or a degree of belief, depending on the situation.

Probability is not automatically the same thing as frequency.

